# QCyberIndia - environment variables
#
# This file is a template only.
# Do NOT put real passwords, API keys, database credentials, or secrets here.
#
# Copy this file to .env.local for local development:
#   cp .env.example .env.local
#
# Production values must be configured separately on the production server.
#
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------
# Database
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------
# Used by Qbids + QFinance registrations/community + unified admin counts.
#
# Required for database-backed features.
# Without it, the application fails gracefully where supported.
DATABASE_URL=

# Optional.
# Most managed PostgreSQL providers require SSL.
# Leave empty unless you specifically need to override the behavior.
#
# Set to "false" only for a local/self-hosted PostgreSQL instance that
# does not support SSL.
DATABASE_SSL=

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------
# Email - Resend
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------
# Required for actual email delivery.
#
# Used by:
# - QCyberIndia contact form
# - Qbids beta registration notifications
# - QFinance Community magic-link authentication
RESEND_API_KEY=

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------
# Unified QCyberIndia Admin Authentication
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------
# ONE password protects the unified QCyberIndia admin area.
#
# Used by:
# - /admin
# - /admin/qbids
# - /admin/qfinance
#
# There is no separate active Qbids or QFinance admin password.
#
# Use a strong, unique password in real environments.
QCYBERINDIA_ADMIN_PASSWORD=

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------
# QFinera Authentication
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------
# QFinera now uses email + password with server-side sessions stored in
# PostgreSQL (db/migrations/010_qfinera_password_auth.sql). No signing
# secret is needed. QFINANCE_AUTH_SECRET was used by the retired
# magic-link sign-in and can be removed from real environments.
#
# Account emails (confirm email, password reset) are sent with RESEND_API_KEY.


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------
# QFinance Application URL
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------
# Canonical base URL used when QFinance generates absolute URLs.
#
# Examples:
#
# Production:
#   QFINANCE_APP_URL=https://qcyberindia.com
#
# Local development:
#   Leave this empty.
#   QFinance automatically falls back to:
#   http://localhost:3000
#
# This is used for links such as QFinance Community magic-link
# verification emails.
QFINANCE_APP_URL=

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------
# Analytics & Tracking
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------
# All analytics variables are optional.
# If unset, the corresponding integration is skipped.
NEXT_PUBLIC_GA4_ID=
NEXT_PUBLIC_CLARITY_ID=
NEXT_PUBLIC_GTM_ID=

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------
# Google Search Console Verification
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------
# Optional.
#
# Only required when using Google's HTML meta-tag verification method.
# DNS TXT verification does not require this variable.
NEXT_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_SITE_VERIFICATION=

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------
# Qbids Landing Page
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------
# Optional Vimeo/YouTube demo video URL for the Qbids landing page.
#
# Leave empty to hide the demo-video section.
# The rest of the Qbids landing page remains unaffected.
NEXT_PUBLIC_QBIDS_DEMO_URL=